Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: "Do Moths Cross The Skerry?"
- Story & Context: When the timber freighter MS Nordstjernen lost its radar in an ice squall off the Svalbard shoals in December 1981, lighthouse operator Einar Holm hastily spliced his Roland vocoder into the emergency radio horn to guide the vessel blindly through the rocks. The freezing brass horn projected his mechanized voice across three miles of roiling brine, reeking of burned tube-grease and diesel exhaust as the ship's bridge crew listened in petrified silence. The vessel cleared the jagged reef by twenty yards solely by tracking the pinging rhythm of Holm's mantra, leaving the helmsman weeping at the robotic radio refrain: "the lamp burns on whale-fat, the moth has no shore."
