Track 2: Alva’s Winter Chrysalis
- Story & Context: Confined inside the solitary iron tower of Røst Reef for three months of perpetual dark, watch-assistant Alva Lind spent her nights rubbing mutton tallow onto her frost-cracked hands to maintain the manual lens pulley. To keep the shrieking polar gale from driving her mad, she recorded her spoken diaries through an EMS Vocoder patched directly into a sputtering drum machine, documenting her slow mental unraveling. Her breakdown peaked when she intentionally smashed the radio room’s mercury barometer just to study the pooling quicksilver on the linoleum, chanting into the receiver: "inside this wool-grease coat I am growing another skull."
