Track 3: Mayflies Weld the Lantern
- Story & Context: Years after the polar outposts were automated, an oceanographic research team anchored in the Jan Mayen Trench began intercepting phantom harmonic transmissions on distress channel 16 whenever sub-zero fog frosted their wire antennae. Listening through hydrophones lowered three hundred fathoms into the black brine, the crew was stunned to hear an immaculate, chorused post-punk bassline interlocked with a dead keeper's synthetic voice vibrating against their iron hull. When the radio operator pried open the deck receiver to isolate the interference, he found seven desiccated Arctic stoneflies wedged behind the tuner crystals as the speaker hissed: "we cast off our carapaces to feed the beam."
